        <div class="prose">
          <h2 id="who">1. Who you are dealing with</h2>
          <p>
            This website is operated by <strong><%= biz.tradingName %></strong><% if (biz.legalEntity) { %>, the trading
            name of <strong><%= biz.legalEntity %></strong><% } %>.
          </p>
          <% if (!biz.legalEntity || !biz.address) { %>
            <div class="callout callout--warn">
              <strong>Business identity is incomplete on this deployment.</strong>
              Legal entity, registered address, GSTIN and grievance officer are supplied through configuration.
              Until they are filled in, this Terms page is <strong>not ready for publication</strong> and the store must
              not take real orders. See <a href="/business-details">business details</a>.
            </div>
          <% } %>
          <p>
            Address: <strong><%= biz.address || 'not configured' %></strong> ·
            Email: <strong><%= biz.email || 'not configured' %></strong> ·
            Phone: <strong><%= biz.phone || 'not configured' %></strong>
          </p>

          <h2 id="use">2. Using this website</h2>
          <p>By browsing or buying, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, simply stop using the site.</p>
          <p>You agree not to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>use the site for anything unlawful, or in a way that interferes with other customers;</li>
            <li>attempt to access accounts, data or systems you are not authorised to access;</li>
            <li>scrape, copy or resell our content, product data or images;</li>
            <li>submit false orders, false reviews, or abuse the support and returns processes;</li>
            <li>attempt to circumvent security measures, rate limits or payment verification.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="accounts">3. Your account</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>You are responsible for keeping your password confidential. Tell us immediately if you think someone
              else has access.</li>
            <li>You must give accurate information. Orders ship to the address you provide.</li>
            <li>You must be 18 or over to create an account or place an order.</li>
            <li>We may suspend an account we reasonably believe is being used for fraud, abuse or to harm others, and
              we will tell you why.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="orders">4. Orders and acceptance</h2>
          <p>
            Placing an order is an offer to buy. A contract forms when we confirm the order — you will see a
            confirmation page with an order reference, and a confirmation message is queued to your email address.
          </p>
          <p>We may decline or cancel an order if:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>the item is out of stock (stock is checked again at the moment you place the order);</li>
            <li>a price or product description was clearly wrong and the error is obvious to a reasonable person;</li>
            <li>we cannot deliver to the address because the PIN code is not serviceable;</li>
            <li>we suspect fraud, or a payment is reversed or declined;</li>
            <li>the order was placed by someone under 18.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If we cancel, we tell you why and refund any amount charged in full within 5–7 working days. We do not
            silently substitute products.
          </p>

          <h2 id="pricing">5. Prices, taxes and fees</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>All prices are in Indian Rupees and <strong>include GST at 18%</strong>. The tax component is itemised
              on your order summary and invoice.</li>
            <li>Shipping is ₹79, free over ₹1,499. It is displayed in your bag and at checkout before you pay.</li>
            <li>Cash on delivery, where enabled, carries a ₹49 fee that appears in the total the moment you select it.</li>
            <li>We do not add handling, packaging, platform or “convenience” fees at any point.</li>
            <li>If we reduce a price, and we show a crossed-out comparison price, it is the lowest price at which that
              item was offered in the 30 days before the reduction — in line with the Consumer Protection
              (E-Commerce) (Amendment) Rules, 2026. At present we run no discounts, so no comparison prices are shown.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="payment">6. Payment</h2>
          <p>
            Payments are processed by a payment gateway. Your card number, CVV, UPI PIN and net-banking credentials are
            entered on the provider’s secure page and are never received or stored by us. We store the provider’s
            payment reference, the amount and the status so we can match and refund a payment.
          </p>
          <p>
            Orders are only marked paid after the gateway’s cryptographic signature has been verified. If a payment is
            debited but the order shows unpaid, contact support with the reference and we will reconcile it.
          </p>

          <h2 id="delivery">7. Delivery</h2>
          <p>
            Delivery timelines are estimates, not guarantees: dispatch within 2 working days, typically 2–4 working
            days for metro addresses and 4–7 working days elsewhere. The risk of loss passes to you on delivery. If a
            parcel is lost in transit, we replace or refund it — see <a href="/shipping">Shipping</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 id="returns">8. Returns, refunds and exchanges</h2>
          <p>
            The <a href="/returns">Refund and Return Policy</a> is part of these terms and sets out eligibility, the
            <%= returnWindow %>-day window, who pays return shipping and how long refunds take. Nothing in these terms
            reduces your statutory consumer rights.
          </p>

          <h2 id="cancellation">9. Cancellation</h2>
          <p>
            You can cancel free of charge any time before dispatch, from your account page or by contacting support
            with your order reference. Once dispatched, please use the returns process instead. We do not charge a
            cancellation fee and we do not make you call a number that does not answer to cancel.
          </p>

          <h2 id="your-responsibilities">10. Your responsibilities</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Give an accurate delivery address and a reachable phone number.</li>
            <li>Check the item and report damage or an incorrect item within 48 hours of delivery, with photographs
              where possible.</li>
            <li>Follow the care guidance on the product page.</li>
            <li>Do not send us identity documents or card details through forms or email — we do not need them.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="ip">11. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The AESTHETICNOVA name, site design, product photography and copy belong to us or are licensed to us (see
            the <a href="/licences">licence register</a>). You may not reuse them commercially without written
            permission. Nothing on this site uses third-party brand logos or claimed association with any other brand.
          </p>

          <h2 id="reviews">12. Reviews and other content you submit</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Reviews may only be submitted by customers with a verified order for the product.</li>
            <li>You keep ownership of your review text and grant us a non-exclusive licence to publish it on the site.</li>
            <li>We moderate for spam, abuse, personal data and unlawful content. We do not remove a review solely
              because it is negative.</li>
            <li>We will not edit the substance of your review. If we remove it, we tell you why.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="liability">13. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            We do not exclude or limit liability where the law does not allow it, including for death or personal
            injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for your statutory rights under the Consumer Protection
            Act, 2019.
          </p>
          <p>
            Subject to that: we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses (for example lost opportunity),
            and our total liability for a claim connected to an order is limited to the amount you paid for that order.
          </p>
          <div class="callout callout--info">
            This clause is a standard commercial allocation of risk. Whether a particular limitation is enforceable in
            India is a legal question we have <strong>not</strong> had reviewed, so it is flagged for
            <strong>NEEDS HUMAN REVIEW</strong> in the launch-readiness report.
          </div>

          <h2 id="disputes">14. Disputes and governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of India. Before any formal step, please contact us — most problems
            are quicker to fix directly.
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Contact support</strong> with your order reference and what you want us to do.</li>
            <li><strong>Escalate to the grievance officer</strong> through the <a href="/grievance">grievance route</a>
              if the response does not resolve it. We acknowledge within 48 hours and aim to resolve within 15 days.</li>
            <li><strong>Consumer commission</strong> — as a consumer in India you may approach the District, State or
              National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, depending on
              the value of the claim. You do not need our permission and these terms do not require arbitration
              instead.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Protection Board of India</strong> — for complaints specifically about the handling of
              your personal data.</li>
            <li><strong>National Consumer Helpline</strong> — the Department of Consumer Affairs helpline, which we
              intend to be a convergence partner of as required by the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) (Amendment)
              Rules, 2026 from 1 January 2027.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Jurisdiction for civil proceedings is subject to the courts that would otherwise have jurisdiction over
            your consumer complaint; we do not attempt to force you into a distant venue.
          </p>

          <h2 id="changes">15. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms. The version and date at the top of the page change with each update, and the
            terms that applied to your order are the ones in force when you placed it.
          </p>

          <h2 id="contact">16. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            <strong><%= biz.email || 'Email not configured' %></strong>
            <% if (biz.phone) { %> · <strong><%= biz.phone %></strong><% } %>
            <% if (biz.supportHours) { %> · <%= biz.supportHours %><% } %>
          </p>
          <p>Grievance officer: <strong><%= biz.grievanceOfficer || 'not yet appointed' %></strong>
             — <a href="/grievance">submit a grievance</a>.</p>

          <div class="callout callout--warn">
            <strong>Owner review required before publication.</strong> These terms were drafted for this build. They
            contain no invented company details, registrations or certifications, but they must be reviewed by a
            qualified Indian lawyer against the actual business entity, its GST registration and its
            seller obligations before they go live. That review has not happened, and the launch-readiness report
            records this requirement as <strong>NEEDS HUMAN REVIEW</strong>.
          </div>
        </div>
<%- include('_legal-close') %>
